<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Mood penalty for unpaid wages (DESIGN.md §39 step 3).

    Situational, not a memory: the thought is true while the arrears stand and gone the moment
    they are settled. A memory would have to be re-granted on a timer and would outlive the debt.

    Deliberately mild. §39 is explicit that "the first missed payroll should not instantly destroy
    the colony" — the mood hit is a signal, and the real consequences are downing tools and
    walking out, which are handled in code.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Intercolony_UnpaidWages</defName>
    <workerClass>Intercolony.ThoughtWorker_UnpaidWages</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>unpaid wages</label>
        <description>I came here to be paid, and I have not been. I would like to believe it is an oversight.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>cheated of wages</label>
        <description>I have worked and worked and seen nothing for it. This is not an oversight any more. Why should I lift a finger for these people?</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-14</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
